From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:19:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: engine info bars drawn by the shell

Plan C23. Chrome draws a tab's info bars in its Views InfoBarContainer;
without a Browser window nothing showed them, and the actions behind them
(an extension's debugger warning, "reload to apply", the PDF offer) could
never be answered.

- OACInfoBarRequest (OACDialogDelegate.h, -tab:showInfoBar:): each confirm
  info bar of the tab's ContentInfoBarManager as a request with the
  engine's message (templates filled in), link title, OK / Cancel titles
  and whether it can be closed. Accept, decline, close and the link do
  what Chrome's views do (Accept() / Cancel() decide whether the bar
  closes, InfoBarDismissed(), LinkClicked() opening a new foreground tab).
  A bar that stays open after an action is presented again; one that goes
  away on its own (navigation, replaced, closed by its feature) is
  withdrawn. The default answer leaves the bar open.
- //chrome's global bars reach every bridge tab (the hook of the previous
  patch): installed at engine start, and each new tab gets the open ones.
